  "body": "Stacked on #2788 (merge #2788 first)\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\n- Each batch prebuild step (`debug build: <crate> (--no-run)`) has the flag `--message-format=json-render-diagnostics`.\n- The executor keeps the JSON messages of that build. It records the test executables of the crate from them (`xtask/src/artifacts.rs`).\n- A suite step of that crate (`--lib`, `--bins`, `--test <name>`) then starts its executable. It does not start cargo (`xtask/src/direct.rs`).\n- The executable starts as `cargo test` starts it. The working directory is the package directory. The args are the libtest args after `--`. The variables are the ones that cargo sets: `CARGO`, `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, `CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH`, the `CARGO_PKG_*` set, `CARGO_BIN_EXE_<bin>`, `OUT_DIR`, the `rustc-env` pairs of the build script, and the dynamic library path.\n- The gate writes cargo's `Running <target> (<path>)` line into the step log. `read_log`, the notes and `--failed` read the log as before.\n- The step names, the step numbers, the log file names and `--dry-run` do not change. `--only` and `--failed` do not change.\n- The executable path comes only from the cargo JSON list. The gate does not search `target/`.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` makes each step a cargo step again.\n- `xtask/src/json.rs` is a small JSON reader. The PR adds no dependency.\n\nThese steps stay cargo steps:\n\n- a `--doc` step (a doctest has no executable);\n- a step that `--only` or `--failed` selects without its build step;\n- a step whose target has no executable in the list;\n- each step of the quick tier, the heavy lanes and the release tier.\n\n## Cause\n\n- `Run::execute` started `cargo test -p <crate> --test <binary>` for each suite step. The build step before it had built that binary already.\n- Each cargo start costs time, and parallel cargo starts wait for the lock of the build directory. The step log of the pin shows `Blocking waiting for file lock on build directory`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all in `xtask`):\n\n- `direct_tests::batch_suite_steps_run_the_built_test_executables_without_a_cargo_start`. It runs the real executor on a fixture workspace. Red before the fix: `post_suites_lib: the step must start the test executable, not cargo`, and the log has cargo's `Finished` line.\n- `direct_tests::a_selected_suite_step_without_its_build_step_starts_cargo_as_before`. It is green before and after the fix. It guards the `--only` path.\n- `artifacts_tests::package_takes_only_its_own_test_executables_from_the_json`\n- `artifacts_tests::package_gives_the_variables_of_a_cargo_test_process`\n- `artifacts_tests::package_refuses_a_build_that_did_not_finish_or_a_package_it_does_not_know`\n- `artifacts_tests::only_a_single_crate_debug_build_with_json_records`\n- `artifacts_tests::a_debug_target_step_of_a_recorded_package_runs_its_executable`\n- `artifacts_tests::the_batch_plan_records_each_crate_and_keeps_its_steps`\n- `artifacts_tests::json_reads_cargo_lines_and_refuses_bad_text`\n- `artifacts_tests::lib_path_puts_the_build_dirs_first_and_keeps_the_current_value`\n- `step_tests::batch_prebuild_leaves_suite_steps_fresh_with_truck_dev_dep` (of #2788) got one line. It sends the JSON output of the build to null.\n\nMutation results. Each mutation was put in by hand and removed again. The pins were green after each restore.\n\n| Mutation | Pin that went red |\n|---|---|\n| `plan::debug_build_crate` without the JSON flag (the old args) | `batch_suite_steps_run_the_built_test_executables_without_a_cargo_start`, `only_a_single_crate_debug_build_with_json_records`, `the_batch_plan_records_each_crate_and_keeps_its_steps` |\n| `direct::of` does not set the package variables | `batch_suite_steps_run...` (the fixture test read `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` of `xtask`), `a_debug_target_step_of_a_recorded_package_runs_its_executable` |\n| `direct::run` starts in the workspace root | `batch_suite_steps_run...` (the fixture test asserts its working directory) |\n| `direct::of` accepts an arg that it does not know (`--release`, `--features`) | `a_debug_target_step_of_a_recorded_package_runs_its_executable` |\n| `direct::records` accepts a build of two packages | `only_a_single_crate_debug_build_with_json_records` |\n| `artifacts::package` takes an artifact that is not a test build | `package_takes_only_its_own_test_executables_from_the_json`, `package_gives_the_variables_of_a_cargo_test_process` |\n| `artifacts::package` takes the artifacts of other packages | `package_takes_only_its_own_test_executables_from_the_json` |\n| `artifacts::package` accepts a build that failed | `package_refuses_a_build_that_did_not_finish_or_a_package_it_does_not_know` |\n\nGate on head `68feacb29`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. 1 step (`xtask unit tests`), 184 s. 201 unit tests and 22 integration tests pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: no warnings.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run`: 929 steps, the same names as on #2788.\n\n## Wall time\n\nMeasured on macOS (16 cores, shared with other agent builds, load about 10), job budget 6, warm build, compile cache off. The selection is 5 build steps and the 205 suite steps of `geometry`, `cl`, `tools`, `post` and `sim`:\n\n`cargo xtask gate batch --only \"debug build: geometry\" ... --only \"sim suites\"` (210 of 929 steps, all green in each run).\n\n| Run | Mode | Wall time | Sum of the step times |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` (one cargo start for each step) | 109 s | 199 s |\n| B1 | this PR (direct) | 89 s | 178 s |\n| A2 | `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` | 102 s | 186 s |\n| B2 | this PR (direct) | 87 s | 173 s |\n\n- The mean is 105.5 s with cargo and 88 s direct. That is 17 % less wall time for the same steps.\n- The wall time is from the creation time of the log directory to the last write of `timings.tsv`.\n- The first direct run of the same selection had a cold build. It was green: 210 steps, 9.8 min.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A full batch gate (929 steps). Only the 210 steps above ran. The `kernel`, `motion`, `app` and `ui` suites did not run in direct mode.\n- Windows and Linux. The issue gives 0.5 s for one cargo start on Windows. The measurement above is macOS only.\n- The post-merge runner (`post-merge.yml`).\n- A crate with a dynamic library from a build script. The path is set from `linked_paths`, and a unit test pins the list. No real crate of that kind ran.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` has no unit test. The A runs above used it.\n- The `gate` skill text (`.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`) still says that each step calls `cargo test`. The worker session could not edit that file. It needs an update.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2788 (open): `Run::execute` and `Run::step` in `xtask/src/exec.rs`, `plan::debug_build_crate` in `xtask/src/plan.rs`, `run_schedule` and `drain` in `xtask/src/queue.rs`. This PR is stacked on its head `1da2bcca2`. The parent of #2788 (#2779) is merged.\n- #2787 (draft, `needs-rework`, `conflicts`): it touches `xtask/src/exec.rs` and `xtask/src/main.rs`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/1951-gate-direct-test-exe.md`.\n\nChangelog: The batch gate starts each built test executable itself and no longer starts cargo for each suite step (#1951).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1951\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
